---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
---

<DocsLayout title="User Management">
  <h1>User Management</h1>
  <p>
    Identity exposes both <em>self-service</em> profile RPCs (any
    authenticated user) and <em>admin</em> RPCs (caller's JWT must have
    <code>role=admin</code>). Admin actions are audit logged with the
    actor and target user IDs.
  </p>

  <h2>Self-service</h2>

  <h3>Get current user</h3>
  <Code code={`curl -sX POST http://localhost/identity.v1.IdentityService/GetCurrentUser \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'`} lang="bash" />

  <h3>Update profile</h3>
  <p>
    Empty-string fields are unchanged — the message acts as a partial
    update.
  </p>
  <Code code={`curl -sX POST http://localhost/identity.v1.IdentityService/UpdateProfile \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"name":"Alice Anderson","avatarUrl":"https://..."}'`} lang="bash" />

  <h2>Admin RPCs</h2>
  <p>
    All RPCs in this section require <code>role=admin</code>. The
    requirement is enforced in the Connect handler and audit logged.
  </p>

  <h3>List users</h3>
  <p>
    Cursor-paginated. Supports a status filter
    (<code>USER_STATUS_ACTIVE</code> /
    <code>USER_STATUS_INVITED</code> / etc.) and a substring search on
    email + name.
  </p>
  <Code code={`curl -sX POST http://localhost/identity.v1.IdentityService/ListUsers \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN_TOKEN" \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"limit":50,"statusFilter":"USER_STATUS_ACTIVE","search":"@example.com"}'`} lang="bash" />

  <h3>CRUD</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>RPC</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>CreateUser</code></td>
      <td>Direct create. Most flows should use <code>InviteUser</code> instead.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>GetUser</code></td>
      <td>Returns the full <code>User</code> by ID.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>UpdateUser</code></td>
      <td>Admin-edits a user's name, avatar, or role.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>DeleteUser</code></td>
      <td>Hard delete. Prefer <code>DeactivateUser</code> for reversibility.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h3>Lifecycle</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong><code>InviteUser</code></strong> — see
      <a href="/identity/docs/auth/invitations">Invitations</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>DeactivateUser</code></strong> — sets status to
      <code>USER_STATUS_DEACTIVATED</code>; future logins are rejected
      with <code>account_not_active</code>. Existing access tokens remain
      valid until <code>exp</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>ReactivateUser</code></strong> — flips status back to
      <code>USER_STATUS_ACTIVE</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>ResetUserPassword</code></strong> — generate a temp
      password (return to admin) or a reset token (admin delivers
      manually).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>SetUserQuota</code></strong> — set per-user
      <code>quota_bytes</code>. Identity stores it but does not enforce
      it; downstream services may consult the field via
      <code>GetUser</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Groups</h2>
  <p>
    Groups are a named collection of users, scoped to a Project. A group is
    stored as a graph node (node type <code>working_group</code>), and
    membership is a graph edge: each member is a <code>MEMBER_OF</code> edge
    pointing from the user node to the group node (not a relational join row).
  </p>
  <p>
    Identity stores this membership data, but does not treat group
    membership as an authorization rule. Group-management RPCs require an
    admin caller; app-level ACL checks such as "only members of
    group X may do Y" remain the calling application's responsibility.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>CreateGroup</code>, <code>UpdateGroup</code>, <code>DeleteGroup</code>, <code>ListGroups</code></li>
    <li>Membership: <code>AddGroupMember</code>, <code>RemoveGroupMember</code>,
      <code>ListGroupMembers</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Status enum</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>USER_STATUS_ACTIVE</code></td><td>Normal — can log in</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>USER_STATUS_INVITED</code></td><td>Invitation pending; cannot log in until <code>AcceptInvitation</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>USER_STATUS_DEACTIVATED</code></td><td>Disabled by an admin; reversible via <code>ReactivateUser</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>USER_STATUS_SUSPENDED</code></td><td>Locked out; cannot log in</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>USER_STATUS_PENDING_PARENTAL_CONSENT</code></td><td>Child-band account created under age-gating that has not yet obtained verifiable parental consent; exists but cannot mint full access tokens until consent is granted (COPPA)</td></tr>
  </table>
</DocsLayout>
